(* The package m5-display: lines of text and numbers on the display of an
   M5Stack core, through M5Unified. Grades: time-interval-rational, in
   milliseconds.

   ShowText s and ShowNumber x write a line, the number with three decimals,
   below the previous one; ClearDisplay () clears the display and returns to
   its first line. The default implementations take the time of the action
   and show nothing.

   PROVISIONAL: the bounds of the running times are estimates for a display of
   320 by 240 pixels on an SPI bus of 40 MHz, to be measured on the device. *)

operation ShowText : string ~> unit # [0.2, 20]
default ShowText _ = delay 1

operation ShowNumber : float ~> unit # [0.2, 20]
default ShowNumber _ = delay 1

operation ClearDisplay : unit ~> unit # [10, 60]
default ClearDisplay () = delay 31
